meta {
  name: Resend Owner Invite (Cooldown)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/platform/agencies/{{onboardedAgencyId}}/owner-invite/resend
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{platformAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 409 inside the per-user cooldown", function () {
    // Onboarding sent an invite a second ago, so this is the cooldown doing its
    // job. It is asserted rather than worked around: an operator hammering
    // Resend must not be able to mail the same person repeatedly, and the
    // global rate limits are per IP and would not stop it.
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(409);
  });

  test("says how long to wait", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().message).to.match(/just sent|second/i);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /platform/agencies/:agencyId/owner-invite/resend — resend the owner's invite

  The recovery path when onboarding came back with `owner.emailStatus: "failed"`,
  or when the link expired before it was used.

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`)
  - **Permission:** `platform:agencies:write`
  - **Data scope:** none — above the tenant boundary.

  ## Why this exists rather than reusing `POST /users/:userId/invite/resend`
  That route is gated on `agency:users:write`, and a platform account resolves to
  `ALL_PLATFORM_PERMISSIONS` and **no** agency permission at all. Without this
  endpoint, recovering a failed delivery would need a database edit.

  Internally it calls the same `UsersService.resendInvite`, so the cooldown,
  token rotation and the "already accepted" / "was removed" guards are the ones
  the tenant's own users list is held to. Issuing a new token **invalidates the
  previous link**.

  ## Why this request asserts a 409
  It runs seconds after **Onboard Agency**, which sent an invite — so the
  per-user cooldown (`INVITE_RESEND_COOLDOWN_SECONDS`, 60s) correctly refuses it.
  Reaching the `200` needs either a 60-second wait, which no collection run
  should contain, or the case it actually exists for: a **failed** dispatch,
  which clears `inviteLastSentAt` precisely so the person recovering from it is
  not told "an invite was just sent to this address" when none was. That path is
  covered by `test/agency-onboarding.e2e-spec.ts`.

  ## Response `200`
  Same `owner` object `POST /platform/agencies` returns, with a fresh
  `inviteUrl`, `expiresAt` and `emailStatus: "queued"`.

  ## Errors
  - `404 Not Found` — unknown agency, or it has no owner.
  - `409 Conflict` — the owner has already accepted, or a resend was issued
    inside the per-user cooldown.
  - `403 Forbidden` — not a platform account.
}
